    "updated_at": "2017-10-06T17:24:34Z",
    "body": "'color' and 'background-color' were made UA-defined for accessibility reasons, I believe.  (That said, the current spec confusingly just says \"the initial value is 'black'\" in the prose; I'll raise an issue about that.)\r\n\r\nWe don't do that for anything else. We only use UA-stylesheet rules when a particular value isn't good globally. That isn't the case here; if we're agreeing that ink-skipping is a good default behavior, it looks like it's good for everyone - that seems to be what the thread has settled on.",
